.TH MYFILEFUNCTIONS 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount, mygrep \- custom file-based utility functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.br
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions provide file-based text processing utilities.
.PP
.B wordCount
reads through the file stream
.I file
and counts the number of lines, words, and characters it contains. The results are stored in
.I lines,
.I words,
and
.I chars
respectively. Returns 0 on success and \-1 on failure (for example, if
.I file
is NULL).
.PP
.B mygrep
searches every line of the file stream
.I fp
for occurrences of the substring
.I search_str.
Matching lines are dynamically allocated and stored in the array pointed to by
.I matches.
The caller is responsible for freeing each matched string and the array itself. Returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B wordCount
returns 0 on success, \-1 on failure.
.B mygrep
returns the number of matches found, or \-1 on failure.
.SH NOTES
The memory allocated by
.B mygrep
for the matches array and each individual matched line must be freed by the caller using
.BR free (3)
to avoid memory leaks.
